{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Devolve rules on firework use to local councils and fund better enforcement",
        "additional_details": "We believe better rules and real enforcement would protect both people and communities including animals. So, we urge the Government to:\r\n\r\n- Allow councils to enforce zones, shorter times. \r\n- Ensure action against adults who buy fireworks for under-18s, including misuse in public areas\r\n- Fund enforcement and provide a simple way for residents to report offences.",
        "background": "The UK Government must fund better enforcement and provide a simple way for residents to report offences relating to the rogue use of fireworks in public. It should also devolve rules on firework use to local councils and run a public awareness campaign on where and when they can legally be used.",
